From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] mips: jz47xx: x2600: SPL: The boot ROM's USB mode when
 nothing starts

When the four attempts ran out the SPL stopped with the watchdog off: a
board with nothing bootable on the eMMC then needed the printer opened
and K4 closed before the boot ROM would wait on J28 (USB) for a
restore. alexshev86's tests in djvalic/kiln-os#68 show both sides: with
the SPL's header zeroed the ROM goes to its USB mode by itself (test 1),
but with both kernel slots' headers zeroed the SPL hangs and only K4
gets the board into USB mode (test 4).

The start after the last attempt now asks the ROM for its USB mode
instead, the way Ingenic's softburn does it (the SDK's
common/cmd_softburn.c: CPM_SLPC = "SWB" << 8 | 2, then do_reset(),
which is a watchdog reset on XBurst2) and as the soft entry seen
working in #68 did (devmem, then Linux's reboot: a watchdog reset too,
ingenic_wdt's restart handler). It is the same reset the SPL already
uses for every failed try. It logs

  SPL: nothing started after 4 attempts (last 0x...): boot ROM USB mode
  (J28); power-cycle to try the eMMC again

and resets 10 ms later. This needs neither the DDR nor the eMMC, so a
DDR or eMMC setup that failed in the last attempt ends the same way.

The scratch pad says the SPL asked: 0x4c00 | the last attempt's low
byte (not a value Kiln, Linux or Ingenic's SPLs write). Should the ROM
start the eMMC SPL again with the request still in CPM_SLPC, that start
finds both, clears CPM_SLPC and stops with the watchdog off as before,
so a ROM that ignores the request can't make a reset loop. Without the
request in CPM_SLPC (a power cycle clears it, #68) the marker is a
fresh start: a power cycle still tries the eMMC again, whatever the
scratch pad keeps over a power-off. A start over USB with spl-usb.bin's
tag is a fresh one whatever the scratch pad holds (patch 0025), so a
restore over J28 runs the normal plan; if that still finds nothing, its
attempts end in the USB mode again. Someone else's soft entry
(tools/bench/ad5x-usbboot-mode) without the marker is a start over USB,
as before.

ad5x_start_plan() takes whether CPM_SLPC held the request, so the
laptop model (u-boot/tools/test_ad5x_start.py) walks it with the rest.
---
 .../mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h     | 64 ++++++++++++++++---
 arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl.c             | 57 ++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h
index f0a41a38..2200c71a 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h
+++ b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h
@@ -16,12 +16,18 @@
  *   bit  7    the slot is forced: not the one the boot flag names
  *
  * Linux writes 0x1a1a, 0x3535 or 0x4343 when it reboots, Ingenic's SPLs
- * 0x4f5441/0x41544f; anything not 0x4b00-0x4bff is a fresh start.
+ * 0x4f5441/0x41544f; anything not 0x4b00-0x4bff (or 0x4c00-0x4cff with the
+ * USB request still pending, below) is a fresh start.
+ *
+ * 0x4c00 | the last attempt's low byte: the attempts ran out and the SPL
+ * asked the boot ROM for its USB mode (CPM_SLPC = "SWB" << 8 | 2, then a
+ * watchdog reset, as Ingenic's softburn and Linux's reboot do it), so a
+ * board with nothing bootable waits on J28 as a108:eaef.
  *
  * The SPL, from the value it finds (ad5x_start_plan):
  *   - fresh, or KERNEL (a kernel was started; this is its reboot or a
- *     power cycle): attempt 0, U-Boot proper if there is one, the flag's
- *     slot;
+ *     power cycle), or a start over USB: attempt 0, U-Boot proper if
+ *     there is one, the flag's slot;
  *   - DDR, EMMC (reset during the clock/DDR or eMMC setup): the same plan
  *     again, next attempt;
  *   - UBOOT, UBOOT_UP, GAVE_UP (U-Boot proper loaded, up, or gave up
@@ -29,10 +35,15 @@
  *   - SLOT, SLOT_UBOOT (the slot's uImage didn't load, or a U-Boot proper
  *     started from that slot didn't start a kernel): next attempt with the
  *     other slot, forced;
- *   - after AD5X_START_TRIES attempts: stop, watchdog off.
+ *   - after AD5X_START_TRIES attempts: ask the boot ROM for its USB mode
+ *     and reset (0x4c00 | the low byte);
+ *   - 0x4c00-0x4cff with the request still in CPM_SLPC on an eMMC start:
+ *     the ROM didn't take it; stop, watchdog off (no second request).
+ *     Without it (a power cycle clears CPM_SLPC; a start over USB with
+ *     spl-usb.bin's tag doesn't look at the scratch pad): a fresh start.
  * Every value but a fresh one or KERNEL moves the attempt on, so within
  * AD5X_START_TRIES attempts the board starts a kernel, or the next start
- * stops.
+ * asks for USB mode, and the one after that stops if the ROM ignored it.
  *
  * U-Boot proper keeps the fields and changes the phase: UBOOT -> UBOOT_UP
  * (started by the SPL from 0xA400), KERNEL -> SLOT_UBOOT (started by the
@@ -63,12 +74,19 @@ enum ad5x_phase {
 #define AD5X_ST_SKIP		0x04u
 #define AD5X_ST_SLOT_B		0x08u
 #define AD5X_ST_FORCED		0x80u
+#define AD5X_ST_USB		0x4c00u	/* USB mode asked for, once */
 
 static inline int ad5x_st_ours(unsigned int v)
 {
 	return (v & ~0xffu) == AD5X_ST_MAGIC;
 }
 
+/* the SPL asked the boot ROM for its USB mode as the attempts ran out */
+static inline int ad5x_st_usb_asked(unsigned int v)
+{
+	return (v & ~0xffu) == AD5X_ST_USB;
+}
+
 static inline unsigned int ad5x_st_phase(unsigned int v)
 {
 	return (v >> 4) & 7;
@@ -91,16 +109,36 @@ struct ad5x_plan {
 	int skip_uboot;		/* boot the slot, not U-Boot at 0xA400 */
 	int forced;		/* slot_b, not the boot flag, names the slot */
 	int slot_b;
-	int stop;		/* attempts used up: stop, watchdog off */
+	int usb;		/* attempts used up: ask for USB mode, reset */
+	int stop;		/* the ROM ignored that: stop, watchdog off */
 };
 
-static inline void ad5x_start_plan(unsigned int prev, struct ad5x_plan *p)
+/*
+ * @prev is CPSPR as found (0 for a start over USB with spl-usb.bin's
+ * tag); @slpc_usb: CPM_SLPC still held the soft USB request as this start
+ * began (the SPL clears it). Started after someone else's soft entry
+ * (tools/bench/ad5x-usbboot-mode), that is a start over USB: fresh.
+ */
+static inline void ad5x_start_plan(unsigned int prev, int slpc_usb,
+				   struct ad5x_plan *p)
 {
 	unsigned int ph = ad5x_st_phase(prev), next;
 
 	p->attempt = 0;
-	p->skip_uboot = p->forced = p->slot_b = p->stop = 0;
-	if (!ad5x_st_ours(prev) || ph == AD5X_PH_KERNEL)
+	p->skip_uboot = p->forced = p->slot_b = p->usb = p->stop = 0;
+	if (ad5x_st_usb_asked(prev)) {
+		/*
+		 * The SPL asked for USB mode; if CPM_SLPC still holds that
+		 * request, the ROM started the eMMC anyway: stop. Without it
+		 * (a power cycle clears it) the eMMC is tried again, fresh.
+		 */
+		if (slpc_usb) {
+			p->stop = 1;
+			p->attempt = AD5X_START_TRIES - 1;
+		}
+		return;
+	}
+	if (slpc_usb || !ad5x_st_ours(prev) || ph == AD5X_PH_KERNEL)
 		return;				/* a fresh start */
 
 	next = ad5x_st_attempt(prev) + 1;
@@ -122,12 +160,18 @@ static inline void ad5x_start_plan(unsigned int prev, struct ad5x_plan *p)
 		break;
 	}
 	if (next >= AD5X_START_TRIES) {
-		p->stop = 1;
+		p->usb = 1;
 		next = AD5X_START_TRIES - 1;
 	}
 	p->attempt = next;
 }
 
+/* the attempts ran out: what the SPL leaves as it asks for USB mode */
+static inline unsigned int ad5x_start_usb_value(unsigned int prev)
+{
+	return AD5X_ST_USB | (prev & 0xffu);
+}
+
 /*
  * The value for @ph in an attempt with plan @p; @slot_b is the slot it
  * boots, once known (SLOT, KERNEL), else the plan's.
diff --git a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl.c b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl.c
index 6c9e0d73..f9768950 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl.c
@@ -22,7 +22,11 @@
  *     After a slot failed to load (or a U-Boot proper in it failed), the
  *     other slot.
  * A failure resets the board through the watchdog for the next try; after
- * AD5X_START_TRIES attempts the SPL stops, the watchdog off.
+ * AD5X_START_TRIES attempts the SPL asks the boot ROM for its USB mode
+ * (the soft entry in CPM_SLPC, then a watchdog reset), so a board with
+ * nothing bootable waits on J28 for a restore. Should the ROM start the
+ * eMMC again anyway, the SPL stops there, the watchdog off. A power cycle
+ * clears the request and tries the eMMC again.
  *
  * Started by the boot ROM over USB (u-boot/USB-BOOT.md: the bench's cold
  * start test, nothing written to the eMMC) it does the same, but as a
@@ -202,13 +206,15 @@ struct serial_device *default_serial_console(void)
  * cmd_softburn.c; tools/bench/ad5x-usbboot-mode). Nothing says the ROM
  * clears it, and it survives a watchdog reset; cleared here, the next
  * reset (a failed try, a reboot of the kernel started) boots from the
- * eMMC again instead of waiting for USB.
+ * eMMC again instead of waiting for USB. The SPL writes it itself when
+ * its attempts run out (spl_ask_usb).
  */
 #define X2600_CPM_SLPC		((void __iomem *)0xb00000cc)
 #define SLPC_SOFT_USB_BOOT	0x42575302
 
 static bool spl_usb;		/* loaded by the boot ROM over USB */
-static bool spl_usb_soft;	/* after the soft entry: SLPC cleared */
+static bool spl_usb_tag;	/* spl-usb.bin's tag seen (and cleared) */
+static bool spl_usb_soft;	/* SLPC held the soft entry: cleared */
 
 /* nothing here can hang: SRAM and the CPM only */
 static void spl_usb_check(void)
@@ -216,13 +222,12 @@ static void spl_usb_check(void)
 	volatile u32 *tag = AD5X_USB_TAG;
 
 	if (tag[0] == AD5X_USB_TAG0 && tag[1] == AD5X_USB_TAG1) {
-		spl_usb = true;
+		spl_usb_tag = true;
 		tag[0] = 0;	/* not again after a reset without a reload */
 		tag[1] = 0;
 	}
 	if (readl(X2600_CPM_SLPC) == SLPC_SOFT_USB_BOOT) {
 		writel(0, X2600_CPM_SLPC);
-		spl_usb = true;
 		spl_usb_soft = true;
 	}
 }
@@ -325,6 +330,22 @@ static void __noreturn spl_fail(enum ad5x_phase ph, int slot_b,
 		;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The attempts ran out: the boot ROM's USB mode, the soft entry as
+ * Ingenic's softburn (and Linux's reboot after it, djvalic/kiln-os#68)
+ * makes it: CPM_SLPC = "SWB" << 8 | 2, then a watchdog reset. The scratch
+ * pad says the SPL asked, so that if the ROM starts the eMMC SPL again
+ * with the request still there, that one stops instead of asking again.
+ * board_init_f writes both before the console and arms the watchdog, so
+ * a hang from there on resets into the ROM too.
+ */
+static void spl_ask_usb(u32 prev)
+{
+	x2600_cpspr_write(ad5x_start_usb_value(prev));
+	writel(SLPC_SOFT_USB_BOOT, X2600_CPM_SLPC);
+	x2600_wdt_start(AD5X_SPL_WDT_MS);
+}
+
 /* ---- uImages ---- */
 
 /* CRC-32 (IEEE), a nibble at a time: 64 bytes of table */
@@ -499,9 +520,16 @@ void board_init_f(ulong dummy)
 	 */
 	spl_usb_check();
 	prev = x2600_cpspr_read();
-	/* over USB: started on purpose from the bench, not another try */
-	ad5x_start_plan(spl_usb ? 0 : prev, &plan);
-	if (!plan.stop)
+	/*
+	 * Over USB (the tag, or someone's soft entry): started on purpose,
+	 * not another try. SLPC still holding the request the SPL wrote
+	 * itself (ad5x_start.h) is an eMMC start the ROM made anyway.
+	 */
+	ad5x_start_plan(spl_usb_tag ? 0 : prev, spl_usb_soft, &plan);
+	spl_usb = spl_usb_tag || (spl_usb_soft && !plan.stop);
+	if (plan.usb)
+		spl_ask_usb(prev);
+	else if (!plan.stop)
 		spl_phase(AD5X_PH_DDR, plan.slot_b);
 
 	timer_init();
@@ -516,11 +544,20 @@ void board_init_f(ulong dummy)
 		       "a fresh start\n",
 		       spl_usb_soft ? " (soft entry, SLPC cleared)" : "", prev);
 
+	if (plan.usb) {
+		printf("SPL: nothing started after %u attempts (last 0x%x): "
+		       "boot ROM USB mode (J28); power-cycle to try the eMMC "
+		       "again\n", AD5X_START_TRIES, prev);
+		x2600_wdt_start(10);
+		while (1)
+			;
+	}
 	if (plan.stop) {
 		x2600_wdt_stop();
 		x2600_cpspr_write(0);
-		printf("SPL: %u attempts failed (last 0x%x): stopped, power "
-		       "cycle to retry\n", AD5X_START_TRIES, prev);
+		printf("SPL: the boot ROM started the eMMC, not its USB mode "
+		       "(0x%x, SLPC cleared): stopped, power cycle to retry\n",
+		       prev);
 		hang();
 	}
 	if (plan.attempt)
